overall:
I checked all 48 items of the \"model\" and \"data\" keys (M-1 … M-19, DC-1 … DC-29) against the code and documents at 6f5b085. Checks run: `cargo test -p wfd-model --all-features` (126 tests pass), `cargo test --workspace` (all pass), and `cargo xtask gen-schema --check` and `gen-ts --check` (both pass). I then deleted the build directory /tmp/claude-0/recheck-model; the working tree is clean.

45 items are resolved. The types, docs, fixture changes and tests match the rulings: ExaltedScaling, the new registry rows, the ability gate, the override-file types with codegen and schema, EnemyDetail defaults, Option<Polarity> maps, STUN_GATED, the opt.rs rules, CondClass::U, ViewEv fields, BuildSpend k, ZoomLevel.enables, GUARDIAN_AURA_IMMUNE, bolstered_og_factor, and the M-18/M-19 doc rules. All of DC-1 … DC-9, DC-13 … DC-29 are resolved too.

3 items are still partly open, all minor:
- DC-10: the primary-fire and \"5 headshot pellets of one shot\" gain filters have no Cond form.
- DC-11: the fixture's Electric Shield still lacks `dot_scaling = false`.
- DC-12: custom p.k is still `sc_mul` in the fixture, no `sc_vuln` group exists, and docs still call the placement undecided after the spec round ruled it target-side.

The deviations from the reviewers' fixes all hold up.

New problems the fixes introduced:
- One major (N-1): the new bundle fields `Weapon.exalted`, `Attack.exalted_s` and `ZoomLevel.enables` have no authoring or ingestion path. No override field, no spec table and no T18 Provides line produces them, so the real bundle would still evaluate every exalted weapon with m_str = 1. The merge note records this as awaiting an owner decision.
- Eight minor:
  - the `strip_ability` doc contradicts the item-level gate (Caustic Strike);
  - `AssembledWeapon.m_str` is per weapon while `exalted_s` is per attack;
  - the §16.13 Primary Compression example names a nonexistent group `compression`;
  - several docs are stale after the spec round (cc_set/sc_set placement, P_5/P_6, the Doughty Step example);
  - class `u` has no i18n keys;
  - the fixture toggle label keys now differ from the frontend catalogue (the mini bundle is the default embedded bundle);
  - the f64 → Option<u8> conversion for the abilityCombo alias is unspecified;
  - the modular and archmelee override directories have no owner.
